{"8":[{"k":"li","t":"2. CIRCUIT DESCRIPTION"},{"k":"p","t":"2-1. GENERAL SYSTEM DESCRIPTION"},{"k":"li","t":"1. The Indy 806 electronics system consists of the following components:"},{"k":"tr","t":"Part/Assy No.   Qty.   Description   Section   Page"},{"k":"tr","t":"A003182   1   Syne PCB   2-2   2-5"},{"k":"tr","t":"A003170   1   Score PCB   2-3   2-8"},{"k":"tr","t":"A003184   1   Coin control PCB   2-4   2-10"},{"k":"tr","t":"A003000   8   Car PCB   2-5   2-13"},{"k":"tr","t":"A003199   1   Backplane PCB   2-1   2-4"},{"k":"tr","t":"A003191   1   Power Supply PCB   2-6   2-19"},{"k":"tr","t":"A000607   8   Steering PCB   2-1   2-4"},{"k":"tr","t":"A003193   1   Remote panel PCB   2-4   2-11"},{"k":"tr","t":"92-013   1   25\" color TV monitor   \u2014   ---"},{"k":"tr","t":"Harness \u00a7& controls   ---   \u2014\u2014-"},{"k":"p","t":"The sync, score, coin control, and eight individual car boards are housed in a card rack within the game. These PCBs are interconnect-~"},{"k":"p","t":"ed by the backplane circuit board which is located at the rear of the card rack. The backplane board also provides edge connectors for interfacing with the other system components through the harness. Figure I-A shows the locations of the various boards and connectors within the card rack. The car numbers, colors, and steering wheel locations as well as locations of the card rack and power supply are shown in Figure I-B."},{"k":"li","t":"2. Basic functional description of each PCB a. Sync PCB This includes the system clock, the video sync counters, and timing function generators, the race track video, the score checkpoints, score video windows, and the ORing circuitry for detection of collisions with other cards. The master"},{"k":"p","t":"audio volume control is also located on this board."},{"k":"p","t":"2-1"}],"45":[{"k":"p","t":"Job Title paceTRAK STEERING PCB ASSY Dwe-P/L 000607 arb Lisl Specification sheet 1 of 1 Drawn Checked Mech, Eng. Rev. ATARI Proj. Eng lElec. Eng."},{"k"